        {
          "description": "<h2>Goal</h2><p>Create a temporary music system for development that randomly selects placeholder tracks matching the current level's mood. This helps avoid getting attached to a single song (\"temp track syndrome\") and allows testing the level with different music while preserving the intended atmosphere.</p><h2>Features</h2><ul><li><p>Music organized by <strong>Mood</strong> (e.g. Underwater, Factory, Forest, Boss).</p></li><li><p>Each mood contains:</p><ul><li><p>Exploration/Calm tracks.</p></li><li><p>Combat tracks.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>On level start, randomly choose a track from the appropriate playlist.</p></li><li><p>When combat begins, switch to a random Combat track from the same mood.</p></li><li><p>When combat ends, return to a random Exploration track from the same mood.</p></li><li><p>Avoid repeating the same track consecutively when possible.</p></li></ul><h2>Benefits</h2><ul><li><p>Prevents becoming attached to one placeholder song.</p></li><li><p>Tests whether the level's atmosphere works independently of a specific soundtrack.</p></li><li><p>Makes it easier to identify the desired emotional tone for future original music.</p></li><li><p>Allows placeholder tracks to be replaced later without changing the game's music logic.</p></li></ul><h2>Future</h2><p>Replace placeholder songs with original tracks while keeping the same mood/category structure.</p>",
          "id": "vpffpf1oi8d7rggycgrj4b88",
          "name": "Debug Placeholder Music System",
